  message is unprotected and its `contentType` is `proposal`, the code
  now throws `ValidationError` unless `content.content.epoch ===
  state.groupContext.epoch`, with a message that distinguishes an old
  epoch from a future one. This closes the gap where the pre-existing
  early guard at (then-)line 194 only rejected `epoch < groupContext.epoch`
  (too old) and silently let a proposal claiming a *future* epoch through
  to `processProposal`, which caches it into `unappliedProposals` keyed
  by that (attacker-controlled) epoch.
