  `test/test-vectors/key-schedule.ts(73,9)` error remains -- fixed one
  new error it caught in `example/state.ts` from the signature change),
  and the full `npm test` suite (44513/44513 pass).

**Learnings for future iterations:**
- `defaultLifetime` and similarly-named "default*" constants exported
  from `src/*.ts` are worth checking for the same module-load-time-vs-
  call-time trap whenever they wrap `Date.now()` or other
  time-of-evaluation-sensitive state -- `defaultLifetimeConfig`
  (`src/lifetime-config.ts`) does not have this problem since it holds
  no timestamps, only a duration and a boolean.
- For a mechanical rename across many test files (adding `()` to a bare
  identifier used as a value), a small Python script with a
  line-by-line regex (skipping lines containing `import`) is faster and
  safer than per-file `Edit` calls -- just double check the import lines
  themselves aren't touched, since `{ name }` in an import specifier
  matches the same identifier text as a call site.
