## 2026-07-23 - US-016

- Hardened four independent decode/encode entry points against malformed
  or out-of-range input, per the audit's "trailing garbage and out-of-range
  values should be errors, not silent misbehavior" finding:
  - `src/message.ts`: `decodeMlsMessage` (the library's actual top-level
    entry point, exported from `src/index.ts` and used by every
    test-vector/scenario test) now wraps the previous decoder logic
    (renamed `decodeMlsMessageLoose`) and rejects (returns `undefined`)
    when any bytes remain in the input buffer after a complete MLSMessage
    is decoded. Verified `decodeMlsMessage` is never composed inside
    another decoder in `src/` (only called from `index.ts` and tests), so
    this "whole buffer must be one message" assumption is safe.
  - `src/codec/number.ts`: `encodeUint8`/`encodeUint16`/`encodeUint32` now
    call a shared `assertUintRange(n, bits)` that throws `CodecError` for
    non-integers, negatives, or values above the type's max, instead of
    letting `DataView.setUintN` silently truncate/wrap.
  - `src/util/enum-helpers.ts`: `openEnumNumberEncoder`'s open-value
    fallback (`Number(s)`) now throws `CodecError` if the result isn't an
    integer, instead of letting `NaN` reach `encodeUint16`/etc. and get
    silently truncated to a wrong value by DataView.
  - `src/custom-credential.ts`: `createCustomCredential` now throws
    `UsageError` for credential type ids 1 and 2 (reserved for the
    standard `basic`/`x509` types).
- Files changed: `src/message.ts`, `src/codec/number.ts`,
  `src/util/enum-helpers.ts`, `src/custom-credential.ts`,
  `test/codec/message.ts`, `test/codec/number.ts`,
  `test/custom-credential.ts` (new), `test/util/enum-helpers.ts` (new),
  `test/index.ts` (wired the two new test files).
- Added tests: trailing-garbage rejection for `decodeMlsMessage`;
  out-of-range/non-integer rejection for each of `encodeUint8/16/32`;
  `openEnumNumberEncoder` throwing on a non-numeric unknown enum value
  (and still handling the known-name and numeric-open-value cases);
  `createCustomCredential` rejecting ids 1 and 2 while still accepting an
  arbitrary custom id (5, matching the existing GREASE-style usage in
  `test/validation/proposal-validation.ts`).
- Ran full suite (`npm test`, 45014 assertions) and lint clean; typecheck
  shows only the pre-existing unrelated `test/test-vectors/key-schedule.ts`
  error noted in the Codebase Patterns section above.

**Learnings for future iterations:**
- `decodeMlsMessage` is a true top-level entry point -- grep confirmed it's
  never referenced from another decoder inside `src/`, only from
  `src/index.ts`'s public export and from tests that always decode a
  complete, standalone message buffer. That's what makes a strict
  "no trailing bytes" check safe to add directly to it rather than needing
  a separate strict-wrapper export.
- When adding range validation to a low-level primitive like
  `encodeUint8/16/32` (used transitively by nearly every encoder in the
  codebase for enum/length/generation fields), it's worth a quick grep of
  all call sites first to sanity-check that every caller already produces
  in-range integers (e.g. via `openEnumNumberEncoder`, tree generation
  counters, etc.) -- otherwise a "hardening" change becomes a regression
  that breaks legitimate encodes.
