  Example/PersistenceDemo ternary, so it appears on both demo pages without
  duplicating markup in either.
- `example/nav.ts` (new): mirrors the `example/routing.ts` split between a
  pure, unit-testable function and a DOM-rendering component. `navItems(route,
  basePath):NavItem[]` computes the three links' `href` (derived from
  `basePath`, same normalize-trailing-slash logic as `isDocsPath`/
  `isPersistencePath`), which one is `active` (via `isPersistencePath`), and
  `external` (true only for Docs, informational -- the component doesn't use
  it for anything beyond marking intent, since `handleLink` in `state.ts`
  already decides real vs. client-side routing per-URL). `Nav` is a thin
  `FunctionComponent<{route, basePath}>` that renders `navItems(...)` as a
  plain `<a href>` list -- no client-side-routing logic lives in the
  component itself, since `route-event`'s existing document-level click
  listener (installed once by `Route()` in `state.ts`) already intercepts
  every same-origin link click and decides real-vs-SPA via `handleLink`
  (`!isDocsPath`). This meant the nav needed zero new interception logic --
  just correct `href`s.
- `example/index.ts`: `App` now reads `state.route.value` directly (auto-
  tracked by preact/signals during render, same pattern as other direct
  `.value` reads elsewhere in this file) and passes it plus `basePath` to
  `<Nav>`, rendered before the `showPersistence.value` ternary.
- `example/style.css`: added `.site-nav` using nested selectors (per the
  house style) and only existing variables (`--color-text-muted`,
  `--color-text`, `--color-accent`, `--color-transparent`) -- no new colors
  introduced.
- Files changed: `example/nav.ts` (new), `example/index.ts`,
  `example/style.css`, `test/example/nav.ts` (new), `test/index.ts` (wired
  new test file).
- Added `test/example/nav.ts` (21 assertions): for both the dev (`/`) and
  Pages (`/webcrypto-mls/`) base paths, verifies the three links' labels,
  hrefs, and `external` flags, and that `active` flips correctly between
  Main demo and Persistence depending on the current route. Confirmed the
  test fails before `example/nav.ts` existed (esbuild import-resolution
  error), then implemented and reran: 21/21 pass.
- `npm run lint`: one auto-fixable `@stylistic/indent` violation in the new
