  panel out of `example/index.ts` into a new shared module
  `example/tree-diagram.ts`, so both demos can render the identical
  diagram from `tree-view.ts`'s pure layout helpers.
- New exports in `example/tree-diagram.ts`:
  - `TreeDiagram` (Preact `FunctionComponent`): renders the
    `.card.tree-diagram` wrapper, `<h3>Ratchet Tree</h3>`, and the `<svg
    class="tree-svg">` -- takes `{ layout, hoveredPath, selectedNodeIndex,
    onSelectNode }` as props, so each demo keeps owning its own
    hover/selection signals and just passes the current values plus a
    callback in.
  - `TreeNodeDetailPanel` (Preact `FunctionComponent`): renders the
    hover-peek key-change-count text or the pinned node's kind/public
    key/JSON/root-note block -- takes `{ detail, onClear }`, where
    `detail` is a new exported discriminated union type
    `TreeDiagramDetail = {kind:'peek', count} | {kind:'node', details} |
    {kind:'none'}`.
  - The three former module-level functions in `index.ts`
    (`treeEdgeView`, `treeNodeView`, `treeNodeLabel`) moved in as private
    (non-exported) helpers of `tree-diagram.ts`, unchanged in behavior --
    including the `svg` alias-of-`html` pattern and its explanatory
    comment, kept local to the new module since only it renders raw SVG
    tags now.
- `example/index.ts` changes: removed the inlined `treeDiagramCard` SVG
  markup and the inlined peek/node detail block from `statusCard`,
  replacing both with `<${TreeDiagram} .../>` and
  `<${TreeNodeDetailPanel} .../>` component usages; removed the
  now-unused `svg` alias, `TreeViewEdge`/`PositionedTreeNode` type
  imports, and the three moved functions. `NBSP` import is still used
  elsewhere in `index.ts` (member count / epoch / group ID lines) so it
  was kept.
- Files changed: `example/tree-diagram.ts` (new), `example/index.ts`,
  `specs/prd.json`.
- This is a pure refactor/extraction with no new pure logic (the actual
  tree math and layout stayed in `tree-view.ts`, already covered by
  `test/example/tree-view.ts`) and no behavior change, so per EXECUTION
  RULES SS3 no new automated test was added -- `example/index.ts` and
  `example/persistence-demo.ts` are browser-only modules that are not
  node-bundled/unit-tested anywhere in this codebase (see the US-001
  learning in this same log), so correctness was instead verified by
  typecheck + lint + an interactive Playwright pass against the running
  dev server.
- Ran `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json`: only the pre-existing unrelated
  `test/test-vectors/key-schedule.ts(73,9)` error. Ran `npm run lint`:
  clean. Confirmed via `grep -n "treeEdgeView\|treeNodeView\|treeNodeLabel"
  example/index.ts` that no matches remain (exit code 1).
- Browser verification (Playwright against `npx vite --port 5199`, main
  demo `/`): created Alice + Bob, started a group as Alice. Hovering
  Alice's "Rotate Keys" button showed "Rotating keys would change 1 key."
  in the Status card and highlighted her leaf's direct path in the tree,
  same as before. Clicking the tree's leaf node pinned a detail panel
  showing "Node 0", "Kind: leaf", the base64 public key, the full raw-node
  JSON, and the root-note explainer text (this leaf is also the tree's
  only/root node in a 1-member group). The panel's "Clear" button removed
  it; re-selecting the node and pressing Escape also removed it. No new
  console errors (only a pre-existing unrelated `favicon.ico` 404). Dev
  server process was killed afterward. Note: editing files under
  `example/` while `vite` is running triggers an HMR reload that resets
  in-memory app state (users/group signals) back to empty -- had to
  recreate the users/group once after the file edits settled, before
  interacting further.

**Learnings for future iterations:**
- CSS attribute/class selectors reliably match against DOM `<g>`/`<svg>`
  elements once Playwright is querying the live DOM (`page.evaluate` /
  `page.locator`), but the accessibility-tree snapshot taken via the
  Playwright MCP's `browser_snapshot`/click-by-`ref` tooling did not
  expose a usable selector for the SVG `<g role="button">` tree nodes in
  this session -- `role=button[name=...]`, `g[aria-label=...]`, and a bare
  `ref=...` target all failed. Falling back to a `querySelector`/`locator`
  CSS selector like `.tree-svg g.tree-node.leaf` against the live DOM
  (verified first via `browser_evaluate`) is the reliable way to interact
  with these SVG tree nodes in future sessions.
- Confirmed a second time (see US-001's note) that `example/index.ts` is
  browser-only/never node-bundled: `example/tree-diagram.ts` reuses the
  exact same `svg = html` alias pattern and imports `htm/preact` directly,
  and there was no existing node-test harness expectation for it -- new
  `example/*.ts` view/component modules only need node-test coverage if
  they contain non-trivial *pure* logic (like `tree-view.ts`'s layout
  math), not for pure JSX/template rendering.
