  `/persistence`): created Alice, Bob, Carl; started a group as Alice
  (1 member -- no Remove Member section shown, confirming the
  `participants.length > 1` gate). Added Bob (2 members) -- Remove Member
  section appeared with exactly "Alice removes Bob" and "Bob removes Alice"
  (no self-remove buttons). Persisted both Alice and Bob at epoch 1 via
  their `persist` buttons. Clicked "Alice removes Bob": Alice's row updated
  to "Epoch: 2" / persisted, Bob's row reverted to "Key package ready" (no
  persist button, matching the main demo's post-removal UI for a removed
  member). Read indexedDB directly via `browser_evaluate`: Alice's stored
  record advanced to epoch 2 (confirms `syncPersistedMembers()` ran after
  the remove), Bob's stored record remained at epoch 1, byte-for-byte as
  last persisted (confirms no deletion/mutation of the removed member's own
