## 2026-07-26 - US-004

- Built the multi-device page's state, its User Management card, device
  creation, and a Status card. `example/multi-device-demo.ts` now owns a
  `createDemoState()` whose `users` map is keyed by client id
  (`Alice/phone`), so `createUser` from `demo-actions.ts` is reused with
  no change: it only ever sees a client name.
- "Create <user>'s devices" loops `DEVICES` and, per device, generates a
  fresh non-extractable Ed25519 keypair with
  `crypto.subtle.generateKey({ name: 'Ed25519' }, false, [...])` and
  passes it to `createUser(state, clientId(user, device.id),
  { signatureKeyPair })` -- the same approach as `createPersistentUser`
  in the persistence demo. Two devices of one person therefore share no
  key material. A `creating` signal holds the people whose devices are
  in flight so the button reads "Creating..." and is disabled rather
  than looking dead during three keygens.
- After creation the person's row lists their three devices (icon,
  label, client id) instead of the button.
- New pure module `example/household.ts`: `selectHousehold(user, users)`
  returns one `DeviceRow` per device in `DEVICES` order, each with
  `clientId`, `created` (has a key package) and `inGroup` (has a
  ClientState); `householdExists(rows)` is true when all three exist. A
  person who has created nothing still gets three rows, which is what
  US-009's Devices section needs.
- New CSS: `.list.households` in `example/style.css`, nested selectors
  only, using existing variables (`--color-border-subtle`,
  `--color-text-muted`). It adds new selectors and touches none of the
  existing rules, so the other two demos are unchanged.
- Files changed: `example/multi-device-demo.ts`, `example/style.css`,
  `test/index.ts`, `specs/prd.json`; new `example/household.ts`,
  `test/example/household.ts`. No changes to `src/`.
- Test-first: `test/example/household.ts` was written before the module
  and the targeted esbuild bundle failed with "Could not resolve
  ../../example/household.js" as the red step. 13 assertions now cover
  the empty household, an all-created household, mixed
  created/in-group flags, one person not seeing another's devices, and
  `householdExists`.
- `npm run lint`: clean. `npx tsc --noEmit`: only the pre-existing
  `test/test-vectors/key-schedule.ts(73,9)` error. Full suite:
  45224/45224 pass (up from 45211, i.e. +13).
- Browser verification (Playwright against `npx vite --port 5199`):
  `/multi-device` lists all seven people each with a "Create <name>'s
  devices" button; clicking Alice's shows the three device rows and the
  Status card moves to "Devices created: 3" / "Created Alice's 3
  devices". Only the pre-existing `favicon.ico` 404 in the console.
  `/persistence` and `/` still render. Dev server killed afterward.

**Learnings for future iterations:**
- Keying the demo `users` map by client id is the whole trick that lets
  this page reuse `demo-actions.ts` verbatim -- nothing in those actions
  parses a name, so `Alice/phone` flows through `createUser`,
  `addUserToGroup`, `rotateKeys` and into the client's basic credential
  identity unchanged. Never add person-awareness to `demo-actions.ts`;
  fold clients back into people in `example/household.ts` instead.
- `.card.status` has a fixed `height: 24.5rem` from a shared rule, so
  the Status card is a tall mostly-empty box until the tree diagram
  sits beside it. That matches the persistence demo before a group
  exists; do not special-case it.
- `.list.users` and the new `.list.households` both rely on `display:
  flex` on the `li` to suppress list markers -- there is no global
  `list-style: none` for `.list`.

