- `example/tree-diagram.ts` gained one optional prop, `leafLabels`
  (`LeafLabelOptions`: `reveal?`, `describe?`). Both default to the
  current behavior, so the main and persistence demos render exactly as
  before. When `reveal` is set, each leaf `<g>` also gets a `hide-label`
  class, and the SVG's horizontal margin grows from 30 to 90 so a
  centred sentence on the outermost leaf is not clipped by the viewBox.
- A leaf's `aria-label` now carries the same description as its label,
  eg `leaf node 0: Alice's Phone 📱`, so a screen reader gets what a
  hover reveals. On the main demo that reads `leaf node 0: Alice` -- the
  member name is added, nothing is removed.
- `example/style.css` hides `.tree-node.hide-label .leaf-label` and
  shows it on `:hover` / `:focus` / `:focus-visible`, drawing it with
  `paint-order: stroke` and a white halo so the one visible label stays
  legible over neighboring nodes and edges. New `--color-surface: #fff`
  for that halo; all rules are nested inside the existing `.tree-svg`
  block.
