## 2026-07-28 - US-001

- Code-reviewed Phase 5 (`6e4e759..ac8bbf2`) and fixed all three issues
  found. The two defects and ten mutations HANDOFF.md already records
  were checked against the review's findings and not re-reported.
- Important: re-approving a previously-removed identity left them off
  the roster forever. Nothing deleted a `removed` ledger row and
  `broadcastRoster` builds `known` as creator plus admitted minus
  removed, so a readmitted member was invisible for the room's whole
  life. `onApprove` now clears the removed row. Probe check 19 was
  extended to cover it and watched fail first against the unfixed code.
- Minor: `approve`, `deny`, `removed` and `welcome` wrote without
  checking the room still existed, where `onMls` and `onJoinRequest`
  both did. A shared `requireRoom` now guards all six.
- Minor: `deliverMailbox` could hand a Welcome to a closing socket and
  delete the row having reached nobody. It now skips peers that are not
  `OPEN`.
- Probe hygiene: checks 13, 14, 16 and 19 closed sockets without
  awaiting; two stale comments named the old check counts.
- Files changed: `example-realistic-demo/index.ts`,
  `example-realistic-demo/scripts/probe.mjs`,
  `docs/implementation-plans/2026-07-27-realistic-demo/HANDOFF.md`,
  `specs/prd.json`.
