  known `test/test-vectors/key-schedule.ts:73` error; `npm run lint`
  exits 0; probe 19/19 exit 0; `npm test` 45679 passing.
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - A ledger built as an append-only pair of rows (`admitted`,
    `removed`) reads as history but is consumed as current status. Any
    code that subtracts one set from the other has to have a path that
    deletes, or the "undo" case is silently broken. Worth checking the
    same shape in Phase 7's membership code.
  - `WebSocket.OPEN` is a usable constant in this workerd build; probe
    check 15 proves it, because a filter comparing against `undefined`
    would skip every peer and lose the Welcome.
  - A guard's mutation test is worth running even when the guard looks
    obviously right: stripping `requireRoom` did not merely skip a reply,
    it made a wiped room broadcast `pending` again, which is the
    resurrection the guard is actually there to prevent.
  - Two review findings this session were reachable only through the
    order sockets close in. When reviewing this Worker, read every
    `getWebSockets()` loop asking what a closing socket does to it.
