## 2026-07-29 - US-002
- Settled carry-forward finding 2b by implementing the gate rather than
  recording the room as open. `onMls` now refuses a write from an
  identity the room has not admitted.
- New pure rule `mayWriteLog(identity, isCreator, admitted, removed)` in
  `example-realistic-demo/room-logic.ts`: the creator always passes on
  the flag (they are never in the ledger, since they do not approve
  themselves), everyone else must be admitted and not since removed.
  Applied by a new `requireMember` helper in `index.ts`, placed after
  `requireRoom` -- an expired room's ledger is empty, so the other order
  would answer `not-member` to a member whose room had simply ended.
