driven end to end through the real `setTimeout` (asserting the open hook
is told `true` the second time), a close during a pending reconnect, and
an assertion that the socket `connect()` replaces is actually closed
rather than left open. Before those, all three mutations survived.

One thing noticed and deliberately not changed, because Task 4 is a
verbatim-follow task: `close()` called while a reconnect is pending
