**Learnings for future iterations:**
- A preact component that calls a hook (`useSignal`, `useSignalEffect`)
  cannot be invoked as a plain function, which is how this suite asserts
  on components -- it throws outside a render. So every view is split:
  a presentational half taking only props (`SetupForm`, `RoomLink`) and
  a stateful half holding the hooks (`Setup`, `ShareRoomLink`). Assert
  on the first. This is why `Room` deliberately has no local state.
- `route-event`'s returned function has `.setRoute(path)`, which does
  the `pushState` and re-runs the subscriber in one call. Do not
  hand-roll `history.pushState` plus a dispatched event.
- eslint's `@stylistic/indent` rejects
  `const X:FunctionComponent<P> =\nfunction ({ ... }) {`. Keep
  `function (` on the assignment line and put the destructured props on
  their own indented line.
- The root tsconfig sets `listFiles`, so
  `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` floods the output with lib paths.
  Add `--listFiles false`. And do not pass
  `--declaration false --declarationMap false` as the phase doc
  suggests: that combination makes `declarationDir` a config error
  (TS5069) and the real diagnostics never appear. Plain
  `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json --listFiles false` is the check.
- `vite build` picks up a `<link rel="stylesheet">` in `index.html`, so
  importing the same CSS from `index.ts` as well would bundle it twice.
  The HTML link alone is enough.
