## 2026-07-29 - US-015
- One review of the whole of Phase 7 (US-010 through US-014), and every
  issue it found, fixed here. Read in full: `membership.ts`,
  `mls-actions.ts`, `approvals.ts`, `apply-entry.ts`, `connection.ts`,
  `state.ts`, `views/room.ts`, `views/setup.ts`, `views/waiting.ts`,
  `client/index.ts`, `entry-queue.ts`, the four Phase 7 test files, the
  Worker's `onJoinRequest`, and `scripts/verify-phase7.mjs`.
- **Finding 1, correctness: a removed client keeps processing entries.**
  `applyEntry` had no guard on `state.removed`. A removal does not empty
  the queue that carried it -- the creator can commit again immediately
  (admit the next person, remove somebody else) and those entries are
  already pushed -- and the removed client holds no key for any of them.
  `processEntry` throws, and a throw out of `applyEntry` is what the
  entry queue reads as a failed commit: it stops and writes "Could not
  process a group change. Reload to resynchronise." The removed view
  renders `state.status`, so the last thing a correctly removed member
  read was an instruction to reload, over a removal that worked exactly
  as it should. One guard at the top of `applyEntry`, with the reason.
- **Finding 2, security: nothing bound a join request's two halves.** A
  `join-request` carries `identity` and `keyPackage` as separate fields.
  The room stores both verbatim -- it holds key packages as opaque
  strings and could not check them -- so the creator is the only party
  that decodes one at all, and it was not checking either. A socket
  claiming identity M while attaching B's key package had the creator
  commit an Add for B's leaf, address the Welcome to M who cannot read
  it, and record M as admitted in the ledger, which is what `mayWriteLog`
  reads to let an identity write to the log. The group ends up with a
  leaf nobody who asked can open, labelled with the name of somebody who
  never asked. `keyPackageBelongsTo` in `mls-actions.ts` is the check,
  applied in three places: `commit` throws (the only path that commits),
  `onPending` skips silently rather than approving (the list is
  re-broadcast, so a refusal written to the status line there would be
  rewritten for ever -- the US-014 shape of bug), and `requestItem`
  disables Approve and says why in a `.mismatch-warning`.
- **Finding 3, a false disclosure.** `views/waiting.ts` said "You can
  close this tab ... the invitation to the group is delivered the next
  time you open this link." Nothing persists before Phase 8, so the next
  visit generates a new signature key and is a different person: the
  Welcome held for the old identity can never be opened, and its private
  half went with the tab. The plan asked for this sentence (phase_07.md
  Task 3 Step 2) and it is wrong as written -- the *request* survives,
  the *key* does not. Reworded to say both halves separately. Left a
  note in the doc comment that Phase 8's opt-in persistence is what makes
  the second half true, and only when the person has turned it on.
- **Finding 4, the item US-014 left here.** An identity in the tree that
  holds no group keys now gets a polite "already in the group" for ever.
  In Phase 7 it is reachable exactly one way -- `joinFromWelcome` fails
  after the room has handed over its copy of the Welcome -- and there is
  already a way out, because a reload generates a new signature key and
  a new key is a stranger the creator can admit. The way out was simply
  not named: the status said "Could not join from the invitation." and
  stopped. It now names the reload. The rest of the item is genuinely
  Phase 8's: persistence keeps the identity across a reload, which is
  what removes this escape, and re-admitting then needs a Remove before
  the Add. Not guessed at here.
- Nothing else found. Considered and deliberately not changed: the
  "Connected now" list rendering raw identities (Phase 6, and the raw
  identity is the point -- it is what the room actually knows); the
  in-flight guard returning the shared `chain` when a control is clicked
  twice (correct, and the window is one commit long); `pushEntries`'
  three states (already documented and load bearing).
- Files changed: `example-realistic-demo/client/apply-entry.ts`,
  `client/approvals.ts`, `client/connection.ts`, `client/mls-actions.ts`,
  `client/views/room.ts`, `client/views/waiting.ts`, `client/style.css`
  (one selector, for the new warning, beside the one it matches),
